    /// <summary>Whether the edit-expense modal asks about a trip at all. Three cases, and only three:
    /// <list type="bullet">
    /// <item>trip mode — a trip is running, so "was this part of it?" is a live question about today's spending;</item>
    /// <item>the row was opened from a trip's ledger, where the trip is the whole context;</item>
    /// <item>the expense already carries a trip — it has to stay visible, or a wrong link would be unfixable.</item>
    /// </list>
    /// Otherwise it renders nothing. The old rule was simply "the account has ever had a trip", which meant one
    /// finished holiday left a dead chip row on every grocery edit from then on. Attaching a forgotten cost to a
    /// past trip still has its door: "Add something already paid", on the trip's own card.</summary>
